# Application Class Conventions

## Standard Application Structure

### Base Class Pattern
```python
class GxApplication(CustomSimpleThreadingApplication):
    def __init__(self, max_threads=1, request_handler=None):
        super().__init__(application_id=APP_3GPP_GX, is_acct_application=False, is_auth_application=True, max_threads=max_threads, request_handler=request_handler)
```

### Standard Properties
```python
@property
def sessions(self) -> Dict[str, SessionType]:
    """Get all sessions for this application"""
    return self.session_manager.sessions.get(APP_ID, {})
```

## Method Naming Conventions

### Session Access Methods
All applications use consistent method names:

```python
# Standard method names (no app prefix)
def get_session_by_id(self, session_id: str) -> Optional[SessionType]:
    """Get session by ID"""
    session = self.session_manager.sessions.get_session_by_id(APP_ID, session_id)
    return session if isinstance(session, SessionType) else None

# App-specific methods (with app prefix for clarity)
def get_session_by_framed_ip_address(self, framed_ip_address: str) -> Optional[GxSession]:
    """Get Gx session by framed IP address"""
    session = self.session_manager.sessions.get_session_by_framed_ip(APP_3GPP_GX, framed_ip_address)
    return session if isinstance(session, GxSession) else None
```

## Request Handling Pattern

### Standard Request Flow
```python
def send_request_custom(self, request: DiameterMessage, timeout=5):
    """Send request with session management handled by SessionManager"""
    if not isinstance(request, DiameterMessage):
        raise ValueError("request must be an instance of DiameterMessage")
    
    # All session management handled by SessionManager
    return super().send_request_custom(request, timeout)
```

